WEBVTT

00:00:03.061 --> 00:00:04.687
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off.

00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:06.762
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:08.076
The family business.

00:00:10.086 --> 00:00:12.135
You still running credit-card scams?

00:00:12.136 --> 00:00:13.529
You think credit-card fraud is easy?

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.632
- Okay, Mr. Burkowitz.
- Federal marshals.

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:17.541
- Environmental study majors.
- I'm father Simmons.

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:19.439
U.S. Wildlife service.
Nigel Tuffnel.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.249
- Dr. Jerry Kaplan. Art dealers. Rangers.
- Reporters. Students.

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:25.372
- Fraternity brothers.
- Homeland security? Pretty illegal, even for us.

00:00:25.373 --> 00:00:28.162
<i>S.W.A.T. team discovered
a local woman bound and gagged.</i>

00:00:28.165 --> 00:00:32.128
<i>Her attacker, a white male
approximately 24 to 30 years of age,</i>

00:00:32.123 --> 00:00:34.711
- <i>was discovered hiding in the home.</i>
- Shapeshifter?

00:00:34.744 --> 00:00:36.791
Every culture in the world
has a shapeshifter lore,

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:40.204
legends of creatures who can transform
themselves into animals or other men.

00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:49.619
Cops are blaming this Dean Winchester guy
for Emily's murder.

00:00:49.653 --> 00:00:51.440
- Sorry I'm gonna miss it.
- Miss what?

00:00:51.505 --> 00:00:53.813
How many chances am I gonna have
to see my own funeral?

00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:07.123
Under what name?

00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:10.487
Oh, yeah, that's my favorite so far.

00:01:11.401 --> 00:01:13.890
Possible I.D.S in three states
that we know of.

00:01:17.531 --> 00:01:18.836
I got to call you back.

00:01:26.224 --> 00:01:27.047
Wow.

00:01:30.018 --> 00:01:32.427
First I thought
you were just stepping up your game.

00:01:33.401 --> 00:01:34.609
Credit-card fraud,

00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:37.434
breaking and entering.
This one,

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.743
a puzzle...

00:01:39.151 --> 00:01:40.639
Grave desecration.

00:01:42.274 --> 00:01:45.295
But still, these are a long way from murder.

00:01:46.521 --> 00:01:48.489
Then we get a fax from St. Louis...

00:01:50.274 --> 00:01:53.764
where you're suspected of torturing
and murdering a young woman.

00:01:54.803 --> 00:01:57.510
However, no one could prove anything,
of course, because

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.275
supposedly you died there.

00:02:02.642 --> 00:02:04.210
But I got to tell you something.

00:02:05.848 --> 00:02:08.037
You look pretty healthy to me.

00:02:11.636 --> 00:02:15.307
So, now we know Karen Giles
wasn't the first person you murdered.

00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:17.880
Going somewhere, Sam?

00:02:19.528 --> 00:02:21.623
But I guarantee you she's the last.

00:02:31.062 --> 00:02:32.568
Transcript : Raceman

00:02:32.626 --> 00:02:34.123
Titelilie
www.forom.com

00:02:44.452 --> 00:02:45.899
Thought you might be thirsty.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.510
Okay, so you're the good cop.

00:02:48.808 --> 00:02:51.367
- Where's the bad cop?
- He's with your brother.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.477
Okay. And you're holding us why?

00:02:53.485 --> 00:02:55.613
He's being held on suspicion of murder.

00:02:55.618 --> 00:02:58.387
- And you? We'll see.
- Murder?

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.960
You sound genuinely surprised.

00:03:01.604 --> 00:03:03.103
Or are you that good of an actor?

00:03:03.117 --> 00:03:04.662
Who is he supposed to have murdered?

00:03:04.668 --> 00:03:06.877
- We'll get around to that.
- You can't just hold us here

00:03:06.893 --> 00:03:10.172
- without formal charges.
- Actually, we can for 48 hours.

00:03:10.175 --> 00:03:12.735
But you, being a prelaw student,
would know that.

00:03:14.221 --> 00:03:15.781
I know all about you, Sam.

00:03:17.076 --> 00:03:18.474
You're 23 years old.

00:03:18.677 --> 00:03:20.465
No job, no home address.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.390
Your mother died when you were a baby.

00:03:23.927 --> 00:03:26.364
Your father's whereabouts are unknown.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.887
And then there's

00:03:27.892 --> 00:03:29.500
the case of your brother, Dean,

00:03:30.284 --> 00:03:33.082
whose demise was, well,
just a little bit exaggerated.

00:03:33.089 --> 00:03:35.155
Feel free to jump in whenever you like.

00:03:37.432 --> 00:03:38.491
Shy?

00:03:38.496 --> 00:03:39.623
No problem.

00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:40.654
I'll keep going.

00:03:41.088 --> 00:03:43.509
Your family moved around a lot
when you were a kid.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:46.321
Despite that, you were a straight-A student.

00:03:46.436 --> 00:03:48.934
Got into Stanford with a full ride.

00:03:52.024 --> 00:03:53.543
Then about a year ago,

00:03:53.546 --> 00:03:55.252
there was a fire in your apartment.

00:03:55.258 --> 00:03:56.627
One fatality...

00:03:56.629 --> 00:03:57.847
Jessica Moore,

00:03:57.993 --> 00:03:59.100
your girlfriend.

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:04.067
After she died, you fell off the grid,
left behind everything.

00:04:04.102 --> 00:04:05.889
I needed some time off...

00:04:07.036 --> 00:04:08.451
to deal.

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:12.348
So I'm taking a road trip with my brother.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.791
- How's that going for you?
- Great.

00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:17.113
I mean...

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:21.610
we saw the second-largest ball of twine
in the continental US.

00:04:22.327 --> 00:04:23.733
Awesome.

00:04:25.602 --> 00:04:28.289
We ran Dean's fingerprints through iafis.

00:04:28.774 --> 00:04:31.633
Got over a dozen possible hits.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.339
"Possible" hits, which makes them worthless.

00:04:34.341 --> 00:04:35.731
But makes you wonder,

00:04:36.004 --> 00:04:38.485
what are we gonna find
when we run your prints?

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.377
Yeah, well, uh...

00:04:40.973 --> 00:04:42.888
you be sure to let me know, all right?

00:04:43.487 --> 00:04:44.511
May I?

00:04:44.575 --> 00:04:46.173
- Please.
- Great.

00:04:52.536 --> 00:04:54.625
Sam, you seem like a good kid.

00:04:54.892 --> 00:04:56.898
It's not your fault Dean's your brother.

00:04:56.905 --> 00:04:58.773
We can't pick our family.

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:02.906
Right now detectives in St. Louis
are exhuming a corpse.

00:05:02.912 --> 00:05:06.001
They're trying to figure out
how your brother faked his own death

00:05:06.166 --> 00:05:08.643
after torturing all those young women.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.619
Dean's a bad guy.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.201
His life is over.

00:05:12.765 --> 00:05:14.614
Yours doesn't have to be.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.219
You want me to turn against my own brother?

00:05:19.233 --> 00:05:22.215
No.
We already caught him cold,

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.549
red-handed at the Karen Giles murder scene.

00:05:27.066 --> 00:05:29.132
We just need you

00:05:29.297 --> 00:05:31.186
to fill in some missing pieces.

00:05:32.114 --> 00:05:33.719
Why would I do that?

00:05:37.088 --> 00:05:39.446
Because I can talk to the D.A.,

00:05:39.454 --> 00:05:41.041
make a deal for you.

00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:43.183
You can get on with your life.

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:45.586
Dean's as good as gone.

00:05:52.261 --> 00:05:55.211
My dad and Tony Giles were old friends.

00:05:55.977 --> 00:05:58.382
They were in the service together.

00:05:58.389 --> 00:06:01.106
We've known him since we were kids,
you know?

00:06:02.325 --> 00:06:04.891
So we came as soon as we heard
about his death.

00:06:09.783 --> 00:06:11.341
Here you go.

00:06:11.936 --> 00:06:14.485
- Anthony Giles.
- Who's Anthony Giles?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.619
The Baltimore lawyer.

00:06:16.685 --> 00:06:18.401
Working late at office. Check it out.

00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:24.138
"His throat was slit but the room was clean"

00:06:25.115 --> 00:06:27.974
- Huh. No dna, no prints.
- Keep reading. It gets better.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.510
"Security cameras failed to capture footage
of the assailant"

00:06:32.377 --> 00:06:34.062
Either somebody tampered with the tapes...

00:06:34.066 --> 00:06:35.545
or it's an invisible killer.

00:06:36.082 --> 00:06:37.179
My favorite kind.

00:06:37.602 --> 00:06:39.070
What do you think, Scully?
We check it out?

00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:40.802
I'm not Scully. You're Scully.

00:06:41.347 --> 00:06:42.286
No, I'm Mulder.

00:06:42.719 --> 00:06:43.955
You're a redheaded woman.

00:06:44.924 --> 00:06:45.700
So...

00:06:46.937 --> 00:06:49.054
It would've been hard for Dean
to kill Tony,

00:06:49.057 --> 00:06:51.196
considering we weren't in town
at the time.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.728
So, tell me what happened next.

00:06:52.933 --> 00:06:54.281
Okay, uh,

00:06:54.627 --> 00:06:56.292
that's when we went to see Karen.

00:06:56.609 --> 00:06:58.378
She was barely holding it together.

00:06:58.873 --> 00:07:01.022
We just wanted to be there for her,
you know?

00:07:03.257 --> 00:07:04.987
Insurance.

00:07:06.194 --> 00:07:08.230
I totally forgot about the insurance.

00:07:09.425 --> 00:07:11.294
We're very sorry to bother you
right now, but

00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:15.320
the company is required
to conduct its own investigation.

00:07:15.326 --> 00:07:17.091
- You understand?
- Sure.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.955
If you could just tell us anything

00:07:19.961 --> 00:07:22.001
you remember about the night
your husband died.

00:07:22.974 --> 00:07:24.812
Tony and I were supposed to have dinner.

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:27.846
He called and said that he was having
computer troubles

00:07:28.197 --> 00:07:29.945
and that he had to work late.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:32.930
That was it.

00:07:34.036 --> 00:07:36.804
Do you have any idea
who could've done this to him?

00:07:37.398 --> 00:07:40.756
No. It's like i told the police. I...

00:07:41.062 --> 00:07:42.548
I have no idea.

00:07:42.564 --> 00:07:44.198
Did Tony mention anything

00:07:44.203 --> 00:07:45.581
unusual

00:07:45.828 --> 00:07:48.094
to you in the days before his death?

00:07:48.912 --> 00:07:50.238
Unusual?

00:07:50.665 --> 00:07:52.681
Yeah, like strange.

00:07:54.799 --> 00:07:56.936
- Strange?
- You know, Karen, weird.

00:07:57.093 --> 00:07:58.820
Weird noises,

00:07:59.164 --> 00:08:01.263
visions, anything like that?

00:08:08.026 --> 00:08:11.017
He had a nightmare the day before he died.

00:08:11.671 --> 00:08:13.740
What kind of a nightmare?

00:08:14.709 --> 00:08:16.814
Uh, he said that he woke up
in the middle of the night,

00:08:16.818 --> 00:08:19.277
and there was a woman standing at
the foot of the bed.

00:08:20.036 --> 00:08:23.373
He blinked. She was gone.
I mean, it was just a nightmare.

00:08:24.311 --> 00:08:25.827
Did he say what she looked like?

00:08:27.765 --> 00:08:30.484
What the helle difference does it make
what she looked like?!

00:08:34.296 --> 00:08:36.674
Uh, it's just our company is very thorough.

00:08:38.219 --> 00:08:40.910
He said she was pale,
and she had dark, red eyes.

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:43.762
So I gave Karen a hug,

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:46.746
told her to call me
if she needed anything, and

00:08:47.514 --> 00:08:48.377
that was it.

00:08:49.223 --> 00:08:50.383
End of story.

00:08:52.189 --> 00:08:54.637
Sam, I am trying to help you here,

00:08:54.884 --> 00:08:57.431
but you have got to be honest with me.

00:08:58.406 --> 00:09:00.414
Now, we have an eyewitness,

00:09:00.629 --> 00:09:02.727
someone who saw two men

00:09:03.132 --> 00:09:06.562
fitting your and your brother's description
breaking into Giles' office.

00:09:06.569 --> 00:09:07.614
Ok, look,

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:11.222
Karen called us later, said that there was
some stuff she wanted from Tony's office,

00:09:11.225 --> 00:09:12.893
but the police weren't letting her in.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.698
Like a picture of the two of them in Paris
and some other stuff.

00:09:17.004 --> 00:09:19.293
Look, it was wrong to enter a crime scene,
but

00:09:19.296 --> 00:09:20.732
she gave us the key.

00:09:33.687 --> 00:09:34.623
Hey.

00:09:35.319 --> 00:09:37.887
Anthony Giles' body was found
right about here.

00:09:38.601 --> 00:09:40.270
"Throat slit so deep,"

00:09:40.277 --> 00:09:42.014
"that part of his spinal cord was visible".

00:09:43.599 --> 00:09:44.915
What do you think?

00:09:44.923 --> 00:09:46.338
Vengeful spirit?

00:09:46.345 --> 00:09:48.630
- Underline "vengeful"?
- Yeah. Maybe.

00:09:49.299 --> 00:09:51.916
I mean, he did see that woman
at the foot of his bed.

00:09:56.227 --> 00:09:57.575
Look at this.

00:10:00.674 --> 00:10:01.950
"danashulps"

00:10:02.775 --> 00:10:04.432
What's that, a name?

00:10:06.082 --> 00:10:07.729
I don't know, but it's everywhere.

00:10:10.719 --> 00:10:14.085
"All work and no play makes Jack
a dull boy"

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.529
I'd say we've officially crossed over
into weird.

00:10:37.775 --> 00:10:39.093
Maybe Giles knew her.

00:10:39.098 --> 00:10:41.897
Maybe it's the name of our pale,
red-eyed mystery girl.

00:10:42.119 --> 00:10:43.218
Well...

00:10:44.034 --> 00:10:45.670
let's see what we can see.

00:10:51.744 --> 00:10:54.043
There's not a single mention of
a Dana Shulps anywhere.

00:10:54.517 --> 00:10:55.784
There's not a D. Shulps

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:57.327
or any other kind of freaking Shulps.

00:10:57.333 --> 00:10:58.318
Great.

00:10:58.325 --> 00:10:59.891
- What do you got?
- Nothing.

00:10:59.894 --> 00:11:04.665
No Dana Shulps has ever lived or died
in Baltimore in the last 50 years at least.

00:11:04.673 --> 00:11:06.521
- So, what now?
- Well,

00:11:06.525 --> 00:11:08.624
I think I'm pretty close
to cracking Giles' password.

00:11:08.628 --> 00:11:10.494
Maybe there's something
in his personal files, you know.

00:11:10.498 --> 00:11:11.807
By "close" you mean...

00:11:12.163 --> 00:11:13.348
30 minutes maybe.

00:11:16.016 --> 00:11:17.104
Awesome.

00:11:18.692 --> 00:11:20.517
So, I guess I just get to, uh,

00:11:21.054 --> 00:11:22.270
hang out.

00:11:22.397 --> 00:11:23.391
That's

00:11:23.446 --> 00:11:24.463
awesome.

00:11:38.469 --> 00:11:39.626
Dude, seriously.

00:11:39.632 --> 00:11:41.208
Alright. I'm gonna go talk to Karen again,

00:11:41.212 --> 00:11:43.349
see if she knows anything about
this Dana Shulps, huh?

00:11:43.635 --> 00:11:44.403
Great.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:46.784
Keep going, sparky.

00:11:48.353 --> 00:11:51.029
Then Dean went back to Karen's place
to check up on her.

00:11:51.168 --> 00:11:52.151
I mean,

00:11:52.407 --> 00:11:54.425
you know,
she had been pretty upset earlier.

00:11:54.441 --> 00:11:56.046
So why didn't you go with him?

00:11:57.325 --> 00:11:59.302
I just went back to the motel.

00:12:00.487 --> 00:12:02.458
How did you know I was there,
by the way?

00:12:02.901 --> 00:12:06.413
We found the motel matchbook on your brother
when we arrested him.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.396
Let's quit fooling around.

00:12:10.832 --> 00:12:13.641
Now, you were with your brother
the whole time you were in Baltimore.

00:12:13.646 --> 00:12:15.656
Why separate now?

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.380
Because your brother left you
to go murder Karen.

00:12:18.384 --> 00:12:22.306
- He didn't kill anyone.
- I heard the 911 call!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:26.030
Karen was terrified!
She said someone was in the house.

00:13:35.389 --> 00:13:37.889
<i>- Emergency services.</i>
- Hello?

00:13:37.892 --> 00:13:39.880
I think I saw somebody in my house.

00:13:39.888 --> 00:13:41.223
<i>What is your address, ma'am?

00:13:41.228 --> 00:13:43.225
It's 421 Clinton avenue.

00:13:44.162 --> 00:13:45.317
Please...

00:13:46.066 --> 00:13:46.929
Hello?

00:14:40.219 --> 00:14:41.427
Karen, are you in there?

00:15:34.506 --> 00:15:35.613
Oh, god.

00:15:48.834 --> 00:15:50.350
Seriously, what the hell?

00:16:09.241 --> 00:16:10.488
Freeze.

00:16:10.675 --> 00:16:11.793
Stay on your knees.

00:16:12.326 --> 00:16:13.723
Hands where I can see them.

00:16:14.099 --> 00:16:15.124
Now!

00:16:16.925 --> 00:16:18.078
Cuff him.

00:16:31.004 --> 00:16:32.450
You getting anywhere with him?

00:16:32.726 --> 00:16:33.613
No.

00:16:34.137 --> 00:16:36.126
Just a lot of wise ass remarks.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:37.138
You?

00:16:37.853 --> 00:16:40.652
Sam's story matches Dean's
to the last detail.

00:16:41.829 --> 00:16:44.047
Yeah, well, these guys are good.

00:16:44.421 --> 00:16:45.597
I'll give them that.

00:16:47.635 --> 00:16:51.676
If we don't get Sam to flip, we have nothing
but a lot of circumstantial evidence.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.979
We got Dean at the crime scene
with blood on his hands.

00:16:55.345 --> 00:16:57.375
Juries have convicted for less.

00:16:57.958 --> 00:17:00.850
Yeah, but, I mean,
where is the murder weapon?

00:17:01.266 --> 00:17:03.824
What's the motive?
You talk about reasonable doubt.

00:17:03.828 --> 00:17:04.595
Diana...

00:17:05.879 --> 00:17:06.816
do you

00:17:06.894 --> 00:17:08.049
have reasonable doubt?

00:17:13.481 --> 00:17:16.432
We keep leaning on these guys,
one of them will tumble.

00:17:16.437 --> 00:17:18.405
And don't forget about St. Louis.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:20.346
I'm telling you,

00:17:20.429 --> 00:17:21.638
this Dean guy

00:17:21.642 --> 00:17:22.661
is our guy.

00:17:23.834 --> 00:17:26.022
I know Tony Giles was a friend of yours.

00:17:26.027 --> 00:17:27.955
Yeah, he was. He was a good friend.

00:17:27.963 --> 00:17:30.652
I know you want to clean this mess up quick,

00:17:31.135 --> 00:17:33.884
but come on.
Tony knew a lot of criminal types.

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:36.429
- Maybe we just...
- "Criminal types"?

00:17:37.083 --> 00:17:41.045
He was a defense lawyer, for god sakes.
Of course he knew criminal types.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.056
Okay.

00:17:43.442 --> 00:17:46.020
- All right. Let's get back at them.
- No. You know what?

00:17:46.217 --> 00:17:48.375
Let them stew in their juices for a bit.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.953
Come here.

00:18:11.433 --> 00:18:14.562
Dana Shulps, Dana Shulps,
Dana Shulps...

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:26.477
Maybe it's not a name.

00:18:27.273 --> 00:18:29.110
Maybe it's not a name?

00:18:29.927 --> 00:18:31.435
Anagram maybe?

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.087
Mr. Winchester?

00:18:49.244 --> 00:18:50.068
Yeah.

00:18:50.276 --> 00:18:51.630
I'm Jeff Crouse.

00:18:52.578 --> 00:18:54.727
I'm with the public defender's office.

00:18:55.931 --> 00:18:57.181
I'm your lawyer.

00:18:57.634 --> 00:19:00.174
Oh, thank god. I'm saved.

00:19:01.731 --> 00:19:04.178
Can I, uh, steal a pen from you
and some paper?

00:19:04.186 --> 00:19:04.981
Sure.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:07.966
Well,

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:08.786
the

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.637
police haven't found a weapon yet.

00:19:11.174 --> 00:19:12.342
So that's good.

00:19:13.088 --> 00:19:14.071
But, uh,

00:19:14.076 --> 00:19:15.554
they got your prints

00:19:15.949 --> 00:19:17.437
and literally

00:19:18.273 --> 00:19:20.011
blood on your hands. And

00:19:20.887 --> 00:19:22.055
with your police record...

00:19:25.265 --> 00:19:26.641
Mr. Winchester,

00:19:27.067 --> 00:19:29.623
- what are you doing?
- I think it's an anagram.

00:19:29.929 --> 00:19:33.300
- A what?
- An anagram. Same letters, different words.

00:19:34.988 --> 00:19:36.243
Could you do me a favor?

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:39.218
See if you recognize any
of these words, you know.

00:19:39.223 --> 00:19:41.652
Local names, places, anything like that.

00:19:42.868 --> 00:19:45.437
Do you understand how serious
these charges are?

00:19:47.012 --> 00:19:49.233
I'm handcuffed to a table. Yeah. I get it.

00:19:49.316 --> 00:19:51.525
Humor me. Take a quick look.

00:19:58.929 --> 00:20:01.369
Well, S-U-P?
I don't know about that, but...

00:20:02.705 --> 00:20:04.041
Ashland is

00:20:04.047 --> 00:20:05.536
is a street name.

00:20:05.809 --> 00:20:07.308
It's not far from here.

00:20:07.313 --> 00:20:08.187
Street?

00:20:10.187 --> 00:20:14.096
Let's start with where you were
the night that Anthony Giles died.

00:20:14.102 --> 00:20:15.669
Can you get in to see my brother?

00:20:15.675 --> 00:20:17.149
Mr. Winchester...

00:20:17.998 --> 00:20:20.465
you could be facing
the death penalty here.

00:20:20.671 --> 00:20:22.819
Hey, thanks for the law review, Matlock.

00:20:23.375 --> 00:20:25.413
But if you want to help me...

00:20:28.289 --> 00:20:30.096
I need you to see my brother.

00:21:13.955 --> 00:21:15.332
I hope that was meaningful.

00:21:16.536 --> 00:21:18.675
But I'd like to discuss your case now.

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:20.898
Sure thing, Matlock.

00:21:21.975 --> 00:21:24.153
You two really are brothers, aren't you?

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:25.875
Now...

00:21:26.732 --> 00:21:27.859
as you know,

00:21:28.525 --> 00:21:30.771
the D.A. might be interested in...

00:21:33.202 --> 00:21:35.276
We need you with the other one.

00:21:43.173 --> 00:21:44.811
This should be nice.

00:21:48.903 --> 00:21:49.979
Counselor...

00:21:51.156 --> 00:21:52.832
your boy decided to confess.

00:21:52.958 --> 00:21:54.295
Mr. Winchester,

00:21:54.981 --> 00:21:56.918
I would advise against that strongly.

00:21:56.951 --> 00:21:58.729
Talk directly into the camera.

00:21:58.737 --> 00:22:00.625
Start by stating your name for the record.

00:22:04.545 --> 00:22:06.319
My name is Dean Winchester.

00:22:07.086 --> 00:22:08.383
I'm an aquarius.

00:22:08.388 --> 00:22:11.097
I enjoy sunsets, long walks on the beach,

00:22:11.103 --> 00:22:12.468
and frisky women.

00:22:13.267 --> 00:22:14.891
And I did not kill anyone,

00:22:15.539 --> 00:22:16.884
but I know who did.

00:22:16.891 --> 00:22:18.459
Or rather what did.

00:22:19.074 --> 00:22:20.522
Of course, it can't be for sure

00:22:20.527 --> 00:22:22.484
because our investigation was interrupted.

00:22:23.348 --> 00:22:24.645
But our working theory

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:26.289
is that we're looking for some kind of

00:22:26.555 --> 00:22:28.121
vengeful spirit.

00:22:28.368 --> 00:22:29.634
Excuse me?

00:22:30.099 --> 00:22:31.966
You know, Casper, the bloodthirsty ghost.

00:22:33.783 --> 00:22:34.971
Tony Giles saw it.

00:22:35.287 --> 00:22:37.455
I'll bet you cash money Karen did, too.

00:22:37.551 --> 00:22:40.057
See, the interesting thing is the word
it leaves behind.

00:22:40.061 --> 00:22:41.027
For some reason,

00:22:41.033 --> 00:22:42.540
it's trying to tell us something.

00:22:43.629 --> 00:22:45.527
But communicating across a veil

00:22:46.250 --> 00:22:47.278
ain't easy.

00:22:47.895 --> 00:22:50.370
And sometimes the spirits,
they get things jumbled.

00:22:50.787 --> 00:22:51.962
You remember "Redrum".

00:22:52.521 --> 00:22:53.454
Same concept.

00:22:54.062 --> 00:22:54.918
You know,

00:22:55.445 --> 00:22:56.849
it could be word fragments.

00:22:57.075 --> 00:22:58.241
Other times...

00:23:01.762 --> 00:23:02.618
It's anagrams.

00:23:03.717 --> 00:23:05.952
See, at first we thought
this was a name, Dana Shulps.

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:08.136
But now

00:23:08.481 --> 00:23:09.867
we think it's a street.

00:23:09.873 --> 00:23:10.880
Ashland.

00:23:11.076 --> 00:23:12.452
Whatever is going on,

00:23:13.538 --> 00:23:17.169
- I'm betting it started there.
- You arrogant bastard.

00:23:17.864 --> 00:23:20.722
Tony and Karen were good people,
and you're making jokes.

00:23:20.727 --> 00:23:22.346
I'm not joking, Ponch.

00:23:24.344 --> 00:23:28.403
You murdered them in cold blood
just like that girl in St. Louis.

00:23:28.411 --> 00:23:29.938
Oh, yeah, that wasn't me, either.

00:23:29.942 --> 00:23:32.572
That was a shapeshifter creature
that only looked like me.

00:23:36.222 --> 00:23:37.668
Pete, that is enough!

00:23:39.483 --> 00:23:40.562
You asked for the truth.

00:23:43.701 --> 00:23:44.847
Lock this guy off.

00:23:57.810 --> 00:23:58.995
What the hell?

00:24:00.805 --> 00:24:02.072
Where is he?

00:24:11.409 --> 00:24:12.225
How did he do it?

00:24:13.069 --> 00:24:14.558
The fire escape's way over...

00:24:16.745 --> 00:24:18.894
- What?
- These two guys.

00:24:22.876 --> 00:24:24.190
Hilts and Mcqueen?

00:24:24.586 --> 00:24:25.452
What is that?

00:24:25.510 --> 00:24:28.118
Hilts is Steve Mcqueen's character in
"The Great Escape".

00:25:26.432 --> 00:25:27.949
Can we make this quick?

00:25:28.066 --> 00:25:30.764
I'm really tired.
It's been a long day, you know,

00:25:30.767 --> 00:25:32.385
with your partner assaulting me and all.

00:25:32.680 --> 00:25:34.769
I want to know more about that stuff

00:25:34.773 --> 00:25:37.214
- you were talking about earlier.
- Time life,

00:25:37.397 --> 00:25:38.875
"mysteries of the unknown".

00:25:39.081 --> 00:25:40.298
Look it up.

00:25:45.049 --> 00:25:47.086
Let's pretend for the moment

00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.781
you're not entirely insane.

00:25:50.627 --> 00:25:54.477
What would one of these things
be doing here?

00:25:54.483 --> 00:25:56.140
Vengeful spirit?

00:25:58.918 --> 00:26:01.555
Well, they're created by violent deaths,

00:26:01.853 --> 00:26:04.712
and then they come back for a reason,
usually a nasty one,

00:26:04.717 --> 00:26:06.885
like revenge on the people that hurt them.

00:26:07.910 --> 00:26:09.809
And, uh, these

00:26:10.022 --> 00:26:11.481
spirits...

00:26:12.516 --> 00:26:14.804
They're capable of killing people.

00:26:20.058 --> 00:26:21.494
Where did you get that?

00:26:27.447 --> 00:26:28.372
I don't know.

00:26:30.159 --> 00:26:31.337
It wasn't there before.

00:26:33.213 --> 00:26:34.692
You've seen it, haven't you?

00:26:35.586 --> 00:26:36.475
The spirit.

00:26:36.588 --> 00:26:37.686
How did you know?

00:26:37.911 --> 00:26:40.358
Because Karen had the same bruises
on her wrists.

00:26:41.315 --> 00:26:44.334
I'm willing to bet that if you look at
Giles' autopsy photos, he's got them, too.

00:26:44.341 --> 00:26:45.959
It's got something to do with the spirit.

00:26:46.282 --> 00:26:47.681
I don't know what.

00:26:52.392 --> 00:26:53.169
I know.

00:26:54.383 --> 00:26:55.661
You think you're going crazy.

00:26:56.257 --> 00:26:57.903
But let's skip that part, shall we?

00:26:58.861 --> 00:27:01.130
Because the last two people
who saw this thing

00:27:01.553 --> 00:27:02.980
died pretty soon after.

00:27:05.099 --> 00:27:06.094
You hear me?

00:27:09.253 --> 00:27:10.921
You think I'm gonna die.

00:27:10.965 --> 00:27:12.264
You need to go to Sam.

00:27:13.460 --> 00:27:14.846
He'll help.

00:27:16.873 --> 00:27:18.413
You're giving your brother up.

00:27:18.866 --> 00:27:21.357
Go to the first motel listed
in the yellow pages.

00:27:21.532 --> 00:27:22.517
Look for Jim Rockford.

00:27:22.523 --> 00:27:24.302
That's how we find each other
when we're separated.

00:27:24.667 --> 00:27:26.103
You can arrest him, if you want.

00:27:26.919 --> 00:27:28.274
Or you can let him save your life.

00:27:46.255 --> 00:27:47.792
These showed up after you saw it?

00:27:47.957 --> 00:27:48.824
Yeah,

00:27:49.091 --> 00:27:50.727
- I guess.
- All right.

00:27:51.723 --> 00:27:53.873
You're gonna have to tell me
exactly what you saw.

00:27:55.028 --> 00:27:56.985
You know, I must be losing my mind.

00:27:58.552 --> 00:27:59.951
You're a fugitive.

00:28:00.003 --> 00:28:01.441
I should be arresting you.

00:28:01.445 --> 00:28:02.734
All right, well,

00:28:02.998 --> 00:28:05.017
you know what?
You can arrest me later, alright?

00:28:05.022 --> 00:28:06.378
After you live through this.

00:28:06.562 --> 00:28:08.501
But right now, you got to talk to me.

00:28:08.696 --> 00:28:09.855
Okay?

00:28:12.393 --> 00:28:13.408
Okay. Great.

00:28:13.682 --> 00:28:15.630
Now, the spirit, what did it look like?

00:28:15.635 --> 00:28:16.893
She was, um,

00:28:17.810 --> 00:28:19.065
really pale...

00:28:19.893 --> 00:28:21.548
and her throat was cut.

00:28:21.623 --> 00:28:24.435
And her eyes, they were like this deep,
dark red.

00:28:24.437 --> 00:28:27.048
It appeared like
she was trying to talk to me,

00:28:27.211 --> 00:28:28.691
but she couldn't.

00:28:29.496 --> 00:28:30.902
It was just...

00:28:30.906 --> 00:28:32.603
a lot of blood.

00:28:34.901 --> 00:28:36.380
You know what? Here.

00:28:36.384 --> 00:28:39.823
I've been researching every girl who has ever
died or gone missing from Ashland street.

00:28:42.131 --> 00:28:43.559
How did you get those?

00:28:43.566 --> 00:28:46.083
Those are from crime scenes
and booking photos.

00:28:47.079 --> 00:28:49.297
You have your job. I have mine.

00:28:50.233 --> 00:28:53.552
Here. I need you to look through these.
Tell me if you recognize anyone.

00:29:06.626 --> 00:29:07.705
This is her.

00:29:07.870 --> 00:29:08.944
I'm sure of it.

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:11.588
Claire Becker?

00:29:12.265 --> 00:29:15.492
28 years old, disappeared about
eight or nine months ago.

00:29:15.499 --> 00:29:16.985
But I don't even know her.

00:29:16.989 --> 00:29:18.898
Why would she come after me?

00:29:18.903 --> 00:29:19.768
Well,

00:29:20.056 --> 00:29:22.705
before her death,
she was arrested twice

00:29:22.709 --> 00:29:23.904
for dealing heroin.

00:29:24.262 --> 00:29:25.979
- You ever work narcotics?
- Yeah,

00:29:25.985 --> 00:29:26.950
Pete and I did,

00:29:27.103 --> 00:29:28.412
before homicide.

00:29:29.086 --> 00:29:30.384
You ever bust her?

00:29:30.448 --> 00:29:31.825
Not that I remember.

00:29:35.335 --> 00:29:38.247
Says she was last seen entering
2911 Ashland street.

00:29:38.249 --> 00:29:39.786
Police searched the place,

00:29:40.315 --> 00:29:41.580
didn't find anything.

00:29:44.130 --> 00:29:45.574
Guess we got to check it out ourselves,

00:29:45.951 --> 00:29:47.246
see if we can find her body.

00:29:48.574 --> 00:29:49.332
What?

00:29:51.850 --> 00:29:53.638
Well, we got to salt and burn her bones.

00:29:54.072 --> 00:29:55.568
It's the only way to put her spirit to rest.

00:29:56.254 --> 00:29:57.472
Of course it is.

00:30:13.528 --> 00:30:15.667
So, what exactly are we looking for?

00:30:15.982 --> 00:30:17.601
I'll let you know when we find it.

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:13.726
Sam!

00:31:24.066 --> 00:31:25.974
Hey, I'm here.
What is it?

00:31:26.300 --> 00:31:27.958
- What happened?
- Claire.

00:31:28.312 --> 00:31:29.950
- Where?
- She was here.

00:31:30.215 --> 00:31:31.241
Did she attack you?

00:31:31.588 --> 00:31:34.375
No. No, she was just like
reaching out to me.

00:31:34.810 --> 00:31:36.790
She was over there by the window.

00:31:48.992 --> 00:31:50.650
Here, help me move this.

00:31:51.564 --> 00:31:52.570
All right.

00:31:53.458 --> 00:31:54.584
I got it.

00:31:59.847 --> 00:32:01.605
Our little mystery word.

00:32:14.107 --> 00:32:15.965
Now the extra letters make sense.

00:32:21.597 --> 00:32:22.844
What is that?

00:32:24.289 --> 00:32:28.091
Spirits and certain remains
give off electromagnetic frequencies.

00:32:29.326 --> 00:32:31.526
So, if Claire's body was here,

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:34.959
- that would indicate that?
- Yeah. Well, that's the theory.

00:33:00.430 --> 00:33:01.525
Yeah.

00:33:01.730 --> 00:33:04.030
Yeah, there's definitely something in there.

00:33:08.822 --> 00:33:10.089
You know,

00:33:10.925 --> 00:33:12.620
this is bothering me.

00:33:12.637 --> 00:33:14.765
Well, you are digging up a corpse.

00:33:14.769 --> 00:33:16.526
No, not that.

00:33:17.803 --> 00:33:20.003
That's, uh, pretty par for the course,
actually.

00:33:20.308 --> 00:33:21.645
Then what?

00:33:21.738 --> 00:33:22.564
It's just...

00:33:23.332 --> 00:33:26.830
I mean, no vengeful spirit
I've ever tussled with wanted to be wasted,

00:33:26.836 --> 00:33:29.865
so why the hell would Claire
lead us to her remains?

00:33:29.870 --> 00:33:31.609
Doesn't make any sense.

00:33:36.641 --> 00:33:37.717
All right. Here.

00:33:37.721 --> 00:33:38.708
Give me your hand.

00:34:13.712 --> 00:34:14.808
Her wrists.

00:34:15.525 --> 00:34:17.790
Yeah, they'd be bruised just like yours.

00:34:29.361 --> 00:34:30.918
That necklace mean something to you?

00:34:32.879 --> 00:34:34.075
I've seen it before.

00:34:35.993 --> 00:34:36.948
It's rare.

00:34:37.464 --> 00:34:39.642
It was custom-made over
on Carson street.

00:34:44.293 --> 00:34:45.721
I have one just like it.

00:34:47.517 --> 00:34:48.834
Pete gave it to me.

00:34:54.288 --> 00:34:55.946
Now this all makes perfect sense.

00:34:56.140 --> 00:34:57.127
I'm sorry?

00:34:57.129 --> 00:34:59.418
Yeah. You see,
Claire is not a vengeful spirit.

00:34:59.523 --> 00:35:00.780
She's a death omen.

00:35:01.557 --> 00:35:02.883
Excuse me?

00:35:03.140 --> 00:35:04.457
Claire's not killing anyone.

00:35:05.821 --> 00:35:07.048
She's trying to warn them.

00:35:09.377 --> 00:35:11.595
Sometimes spirits,
they don't want vengeance.

00:35:11.602 --> 00:35:14.310
They want justice, which is why
she led us here in the first place.

00:35:14.316 --> 00:35:16.444
She wants us to know who her killer is.

00:35:21.285 --> 00:35:23.831
Detective, how much do you know
about your partner?

00:35:27.184 --> 00:35:29.480
- Oh, my god.
- What?

00:35:31.058 --> 00:35:32.744
About a year ago,

00:35:32.930 --> 00:35:35.720
some heroin went missing from lockup.

00:35:36.046 --> 00:35:37.682
Obviously it was a cop.

00:35:38.377 --> 00:35:39.973
We never found out who did it.

00:35:41.413 --> 00:35:44.783
But whoever did it would need someone
to fence their product.

00:35:44.836 --> 00:35:46.232
Somebody like a heroin dealer.

00:35:48.271 --> 00:35:49.396
Somebody like Claire.

00:35:54.922 --> 00:35:57.469
So, I'm being extradited to St. Louis, huh?

00:36:00.459 --> 00:36:04.420
You just decided to transfer me yourself
800 miles at 2:00 in the morning?

00:36:09.510 --> 00:36:10.809
This can't be good.

00:36:11.623 --> 00:36:13.050
All right. Thanks.

00:36:13.797 --> 00:36:14.621
What is it?

00:36:14.807 --> 00:36:16.327
Pete just left the precinct.

00:36:16.559 --> 00:36:17.968
- With Dean.
- What?!

00:36:17.971 --> 00:36:21.382
He said the prisoner had to be transferred,
and he just took him.

00:36:21.386 --> 00:36:24.356
Dispatch has been calling,
but he won't answer the radio.

00:36:24.370 --> 00:36:25.437
Radio?

00:36:25.444 --> 00:36:27.519
- He took a county vehicle?
- Yeah.

00:36:27.524 --> 00:36:29.984
Then it should have a lojack.
You just got to get it turned on.

00:36:44.641 --> 00:36:45.624
Pee break?

00:36:45.691 --> 00:36:46.799
So soon?

00:36:47.465 --> 00:36:49.370
I think you might want
to get your prostate checked.

00:36:59.039 --> 00:37:00.427
Son of a bitch.

00:37:03.634 --> 00:37:06.014
Hey, I'm cool in the van.
You go do what you got to do.

00:37:11.216 --> 00:37:13.003
You're a cocky son of a bitch.

00:37:14.169 --> 00:37:17.400
You think those people in St. Louis
are gonna buy that crap you're paddling?

00:37:18.254 --> 00:37:19.611
Here's the thing.

00:37:20.139 --> 00:37:22.025
You're not gonna make it to St. Louis.

00:37:23.183 --> 00:37:24.410
You're gonna die

00:37:24.784 --> 00:37:26.120
trying to escape.

00:37:28.942 --> 00:37:30.278
Wait! Wait!

00:37:31.923 --> 00:37:33.161
Let's talk about this.

00:37:33.167 --> 00:37:35.002
You don't want to do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:37:36.771 --> 00:37:38.257
- Or maybe you do.
- Pete!

00:37:38.753 --> 00:37:39.880
Put the gun down.

00:37:40.146 --> 00:37:41.044
Diana?

00:37:41.887 --> 00:37:42.865
How'd you find me?

00:37:43.532 --> 00:37:44.797
I know about Claire.

00:37:44.801 --> 00:37:46.149
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:37:46.156 --> 00:37:47.983
Put the gun down!

00:37:47.987 --> 00:37:49.525
No, I don't think so.

00:37:50.239 --> 00:37:51.308
You're fast.

00:37:51.531 --> 00:37:53.269
Pretty sure I'm faster.

00:37:54.566 --> 00:37:55.582
Why are you doing this?

00:37:55.929 --> 00:37:57.455
I didn't do anything, Diana.

00:37:57.969 --> 00:37:59.397
It's a little late for that.

00:38:00.566 --> 00:38:01.910
It wasn't my fault.

00:38:02.806 --> 00:38:05.484
Claire was gonna turn me in.
I had no choice.

00:38:05.492 --> 00:38:06.558
And Tony?

00:38:06.931 --> 00:38:07.838
Karen?

00:38:07.944 --> 00:38:09.130
Same thing.

00:38:09.536 --> 00:38:11.945
Tony scrubbed the money.
Then he got skittish.

00:38:11.961 --> 00:38:13.766
And then he wanted to come clean.

00:38:13.771 --> 00:38:15.558
I'm sure he told Karen everything.

00:38:16.316 --> 00:38:18.455
It was a mess. I had to clean it up.

00:38:19.620 --> 00:38:20.676
I just panicked.

00:38:20.892 --> 00:38:23.270
How many more people
are gonna die over this, Pete?

00:38:23.277 --> 00:38:24.734
There's a way out.

00:38:26.278 --> 00:38:28.827
This Dean kid is a friggin' gift.

00:38:29.252 --> 00:38:31.233
We can pin the whole thing on him.

00:38:31.437 --> 00:38:35.526
Okay? No trial, nothing.
Just one more dead scumbag.

00:38:35.534 --> 00:38:36.488
Hey!

00:38:39.006 --> 00:38:40.284
No one will question it.

00:38:41.111 --> 00:38:42.949
Diana, please.

00:38:43.394 --> 00:38:44.780
I still love you.

00:38:51.193 --> 00:38:52.270
Thank you.

00:38:54.220 --> 00:38:55.355
Thank you.

00:39:04.691 --> 00:39:07.861
Then why don't you buy me another necklace,
you ass?

00:39:10.582 --> 00:39:12.697
Don't do it. Don't do it.

00:40:02.772 --> 00:40:03.859
You're doing all right?

00:40:05.058 --> 00:40:06.064
Not really.

00:40:07.330 --> 00:40:08.957
The death omen, Claire,

00:40:09.921 --> 00:40:11.319
what happens to her now?

00:40:11.514 --> 00:40:12.602
It should be over.

00:40:13.328 --> 00:40:14.694
She should be at rest.

00:40:16.431 --> 00:40:17.440
So, uh,

00:40:17.935 --> 00:40:19.289
what now, officer?

00:40:19.726 --> 00:40:21.335
Pete did confess to me.

00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:23.757
He screwed up both your cases royally.

00:40:23.834 --> 00:40:27.130
I'd say there's a good chance
that we can get your cases dismissed.

00:40:27.138 --> 00:40:29.774
- You could take care of that for us?
- I hope so.

00:40:29.971 --> 00:40:32.027
But the St. Louis murder charges?

00:40:32.315 --> 00:40:33.941
That's another story.

00:40:34.388 --> 00:40:36.055
I.. I can't help you.

00:40:37.651 --> 00:40:39.108
Unless

00:40:39.255 --> 00:40:42.112
I just happened to turn my back
and you walked away.

00:40:42.117 --> 00:40:44.257
I could tell them
that the suspects escaped.

00:40:44.390 --> 00:40:46.529
- Wait. Are you sure?
- Yeah, she's sure, Sam.

00:40:46.534 --> 00:40:49.394
You could lose your job over
something like that.

00:40:49.868 --> 00:40:52.506
Look, I just want you guys out there,
doing what you do best.

00:40:52.510 --> 00:40:53.408
Trust me.

00:40:53.652 --> 00:40:54.910
I'll sleep better at night.

00:40:56.045 --> 00:40:57.345
Listen, you need to watch your back.

00:40:57.360 --> 00:40:59.376
They're gonna be looking for both of you
right now.

00:41:00.333 --> 00:41:01.298
Get out of here.

00:41:01.803 --> 00:41:04.073
- I got to radio this in.
- Hey, uh...

00:41:04.558 --> 00:41:06.977
You wouldn't happen to know where
my car is by chance?

00:41:06.980 --> 00:41:09.780
It's at the impound yard on Robertson.

00:41:10.908 --> 00:41:11.994
Don't

00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:15.308
- even think about it.
- It's okay. It's all right. Don't worry.

00:41:15.583 --> 00:41:18.113
We'll just improvise.
We're pretty good at that.

00:41:18.116 --> 00:41:19.845
Yeah. I've noticed.

00:41:25.619 --> 00:41:27.495
- Nice lady.
- Yeah, for a cop.

00:41:28.540 --> 00:41:30.030
Did she look familiar to you?

00:41:30.035 --> 00:41:30.910
No. Why?

00:41:31.136 --> 00:41:33.112
I don't know. It's nothing.
Hey, you hungry?

00:41:33.118 --> 00:41:33.873
No.

00:41:33.880 --> 00:41:36.087
I have some reason
I could really go for some pea soup.

00:00:03.562 --> 00:00:05.064
